Only files receive read-only permissions; their parent directories remain writable. Because rustc and compile-time code inherit the stabilized `OUT_DIR`, they can unlink and replace a generated file through its writable parent. `stabilize` then trusts the existing digest-named directory without revalidating it, so later checkouts can compile or restore artifacts from modified sources that no longer match the directory digest. The published directory hierarchy must also be immutable while still allowing GC to remove it safely.

