{"body":"<a href="#"><img alt="P2" src="https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9" align="top"></a> **Generated bytes escape budget**

Generated-tree removals are credited to GC accounting, but surviving generated trees are omitted from the combined-size budget because `target_budget` still reserves only `incremental_remaining`. When `max_total_bytes` is the limiting setting, GC can retain targets as though `generated.remaining_bytes` used no space and finish above the configured combined limit by that amount. Include the remaining generated bytes in both manual and automatic budget calculations.

